WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:01.420
Let's try.

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:08.290
Why don't we go to Sam from Princeton, Massachusetts,
not Princeton, New Jersey.

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:16.360
Yes, I can, so I'll preface this by saying
I sort of realized that this isn't exactly

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:22.350
the type of priorities right now, OK, but
I was just on Twitter before I came in this

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:26.410
lobby and I'm seeing there's lawmakers in
sort of some sort of congressional meeting.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:34.300
And I've seen it going on a little bit, talking
about trans people in athletics and sort of

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.559
legislating that process.

00:00:37.559 --> 00:00:39.149
Now I'm on the left.

00:00:39.149 --> 00:00:43.309
I consider myself to be ardently pro trans
rights and everything.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:50.069
But it does at the same time seem pretty deeply
unfair to me that to allow, you know, people

00:00:50.069 --> 00:00:55.190
who are born just biologically different to,
for example, trans women to participate in

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:57.289
men's sports and women's sports.

00:00:57.289 --> 00:01:01.469
Yeah, but I mean, listen, it sounds like we
have the same view I've talked about this

00:01:01.469 --> 00:01:06.210
before, which is I have a problem with people
that pretend like this is the big issue, the

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:07.600
big injustice that's going on.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.240
And it sounds like you're saying the same
thing.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:12.020
You recognize this is not like the biggest
issue.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:15.630
At the same time, when I think about a sport
like weightlifting or wrestling and I think

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:22.729
about someone born biologically male and then
saying, well, they now that they identify

00:01:22.729 --> 00:01:28.750
as as a woman and they're going to participate
in wrestling or weightlifting, it strikes

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:31.970
me as not making complete and total sense.

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:36.829
And this does not in any way affect the fact
that I believe trans folks should be able

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:40.049
to live lives free of discrimination.

00:01:40.049 --> 00:01:44.909
They should be included in protections when
it comes to employment and should be able

00:01:44.909 --> 00:01:53.109
to have a license that reflects their gender
as as they want to exist in the world.

00:01:53.109 --> 00:01:54.289
And yet it just doesn't.

00:01:54.289 --> 00:01:58.749
I just don't understand how you say, well,
someone born biologically male can participate

00:01:58.749 --> 00:02:00.119
in women's wrestling.

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:01.499
I don't I don't get it.

00:02:01.499 --> 00:02:02.499
I get that.

00:02:02.499 --> 00:02:04.369
You're not saying it's the most important
issue.

00:02:04.369 --> 00:02:05.369
Neither am I.

00:02:05.369 --> 00:02:09.039
It's not even the most important issue within
trans rights to me.

00:02:09.039 --> 00:02:11.430
There are so many more important issues with
interest rates.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.030
But yeah, I'm basically with you.

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:16.530
I would love somebody to explain it to me.

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:17.530
Yeah, I totally.

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:20.870
And the thing that sort of concerns me is
like I because I, I watch your show and I

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:22.370
watch other things too.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:27.069
And the sense that I get is that I would be
called a transfer for that.

00:02:27.069 --> 00:02:31.331
You know, I'm seeing people like in the majority
report and that sort of thing saying, you

00:02:31.331 --> 00:02:36.549
know, that opinion people are sort of dunking
on like Tulsi Gabbard for having that opinion,

00:02:36.549 --> 00:02:37.549
saying she's not really on the left.

00:02:37.549 --> 00:02:40.020
And I was thinking, well, I mean, I don't
know if that's fair, you know?

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:41.020
Well, here's the thing.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:44.230
I mean, the question is.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:51.060
So I've said before how you can be in favor
of the movement to boycott Israeli products

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:56.780
and services without being anti-Semitic, but
it also is a great cover for lots of anti-Semitic

00:02:56.780 --> 00:03:04.659
folks, much, much the same way you can have
this position or these questions about the

00:03:04.659 --> 00:03:10.760
trans women's sports issues and be using it
as a cover for your transphobia or not.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:16.170
You might be a staunch defender of trans rights
and anti trans discrimination and still have

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:17.170
that question.

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:21.730
So it's not a rule that that you are or are
not trans phobic because you are trying to

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:23.950
better understand this issue, as I am.

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:24.950
Right.

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:26.220
That's where I see myself.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.220
So, yeah.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:28.590
Anyway, thanks for taking my call.

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:29.590
All right.

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:30.590
My pleasure.

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:31.870
Appreciate the call very, very much.

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:33.969
That is all the time we have for today.

00:03:33.969 --> 00:03:34.969
I apologize.

00:03:34.969 --> 00:03:39.650
I was not able to get to everybody, but I
hope to be able to at some point in the future.

